Add --codec to ModelQuantizer

Replaces the per-version recipe's codec for the matmul bulk only, which is the
same split the app's three quantize actions make. Convolutions, ada_ln
projections, embedders and 1-D tensors keep the recipe's own codecs, so this is
upstream's own factorization rather than a new one. Sixteen call sites route
through a bulkCodec helper that returns the recipe's literal unless overridden,
and default reproduces current output byte for byte.

Palettizing is DP-bound and takes hours on a 22B DiT where i8x is about eight
passes per row, so this turns quantize-overnight-before-you-can-test into a few
minutes. The i8x artifact is separately the only encoding an Apple Neural
Engine can consume, which is worth having on its own account.

Only plain i8x is validated here. The K-quant subtypes are plumbed end to end
but unexercised, and the iq* formats are importance-matrix quants by
construction while this flag passes no imatrix, so they run at their worst.
